Usage:
  {TOOL} [flags]
  {TOOL} [command]

Available Commands:
  avenue       PROPOSE a line of inquiry (--line "<approach>" --hypothesis "<what would be true if it pays off>" [--status] [--method]; the tool assigns its id), or MOVE one you already proposed (--id A1 --status proposed|pursued|declined|abandoned --reason "<what changed>")
  cite         cite a source at a quoted sentence — the tool fetches, caches, and splices an invisible immortal anchor; you never type a footnote: --location "<the exact sentence, quoted from the report and nothing else — NOT a heading plus a sentence, it is matched literally>" --url <u> --title <t> [--claim "..."] [--key <your C1>]
  claim-index  locate every site of each FOOTNOTED claim in your report (read-only)
  closing      a ### BLUE CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  edit         replace an exact span in blue/report.md, preserving red's finding-markers: --key <your F1> --old "<exact current span>" --new "<replacement>" --reason "..."
  friction     a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  manifest-row one correctness-manifest receipt per repaired gap: --id R2-3 --row "figures recomputed; acceptance check run: pass; sites swept: S2,S4"
  position     the round's ### BLUE section (prose via --reason)
  prove        settle a claim by COMPUTING it: --location "<the exact sentence>" --script <path under the run dir> [--cites <the method's citation label>] — the tool runs it twice, caches the script and its output, and splices an invisible proof anchor at that sentence
  register     FIRST ACTION at the seat: `register`, with no flags — the engine injects your run and your identity, and a --run or --seat-id that disagrees with the dispatch is refused rather than obeyed
  retire       remove a claim from the report, on the record: --claim "<the claim, quoted>" --reason "..." [--superseded-by "<the claim that replaces it>"]
  revision     the round-record event (the CHANGELOG entry body via --reason) — singleton per seat-round; emit AFTER your report edits land
  show         read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | worklist | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry

