  friction    a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  halt        the safety boundary: --reason <written opinion — capture relays it like a FAIL, never smoothed>
  opinion     a ruling as an OPINION: --id R3-2 --as carried|closed|... --principle "..." --tension "correctness vs economy" --review-flag "why a human should look" --reason <rationale>
  outcome     record the run's terminal verdict as a fact: --as VERIFIED|CEILING|HALTED|UNVERIFIED --reason "<how the run ended, in your words>" [--deadlocked] [--exhausted]
  register    FIRST ACTION at the sitting: `register`, with no flags — the engine injects your run and your identity, and a --run or --seat-id that disagrees with the dispatch is refused rather than obeyed
  show        read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | worklist | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry

